PHASE 1 — Unify Design Tokens (extend existing if present)
========================
Goal: One single source of truth for colors + layout tokens + typography tokens.

If token files already exist:
- Extend them to a semantic role-based system rather than creating a new token module.
- If they are scattered, consolidate into one canonical module and re-export from old paths to avoid breaking imports.

Tokens MUST include:

A) Color roles (semantic roles; components never use raw palette values)
- background, surface-0/1/2 (page/card/modal)
- text-primary/secondary/tertiary/inverse
- border-subtle/border-strong/divider
- accent + accent-foreground + accent-muted
- overlay/scrim
- status: success/warning/error/info (+ subtle bg + foreground)
- interactive states: pressed, selected, disabled, focus-ring
- icon-default, icon-muted

Color rules:
- Neutral-driven palette + ONE accent.
- Avoid pure #000/#FFF for large surfaces.
- No funky saturated backgrounds except CTA accents.

B) Layout tokens
- spacing scale (4,8,12,16,20,24,32…)
- radii scale
- elevation/shadows (or border-only strategy)
- screen gutters + safe area rules
- sizing: button heights, input heights, icon sizes, avatar sizes
- typography: title/section/body/caption + line heights/weights

Hard rule:
- No hex/rgb/hsl and no magic spacing/font values in components after migration (only tokens).

========================
PHASE 2 — Unify Theme Access (reuse existing provider/hook if present)
========================
If a ThemeProvider/useTheme exists:
- Upgrade it to expose semantic tokens (light/dark) and persist user preference.
- Keep its API stable where possible.
If none exists:
- Create it once, as the canonical theme system.

Must support:
- system theme
- user override toggle
- persistence
- token access pattern (e.g., theme.colors.roleName)

========================
PHASE 3 — Upgrade Existing Primitives (NO duplicate components)
========================
For each primitive (Button, Card, Text, Input, Icon wrapper, Avatar/ProfileIcon, ScreenContainer):
- Locate existing implementation
- Refactor IN PLACE to use tokens + consistent states/sizing
- If replacement is unavoidable:
  - Create a temporary compat wrapper that maps old props -> new behavior
  - Migrate usages and delete the old implementation by the end of Phase 5 (no long-term parallel)

Required primitives behavior:
- Button: variants + sizes + pressed/disabled/loading/selected
- Card: surface levels + padding variants + radius tokens
- Text: typography tokens + semantic colors
- Input: label/help/error + consistent spacing
- Icon wrapper: token-based colors/sizes; remove hardcoded fills where possible
- Avatar/ProfileIcon: consistent sizes, ring/border tokens, fallbacks
- ScreenContainer/Page: standard gutters/padding/safe area

