========================
**Enforced starting 2026-01-28 per user feedback on visual consistency.**

### 1. Screen Horizontal Padding
- **`screenGutter: 16px`** (reduced from 24px - user feedback: "too much padding")
- Applied automatically by `ScreenWrapper` component
- All screens using `ScreenWrapper` get consistent horizontal padding
- **DO NOT** add additional `paddingHorizontal` inside screens unless absolutely necessary

### 2. Header-to-Content Gap
- **`headerContentGap: 16px`** - Standard top margin for first content element after Header
- **MUST BE CONSISTENT** across all screens
- Examples:
  - ✅ HomeScreen: `balanceSection` has `paddingTop: theme.spacing.base` (16px)
  - ✅ ChoreListScreen: `statsCardWrapper` has `marginTop: theme.spacing.headerContentGap` (16px)
  - ❌ Any screen missing this gap: Must add it

### 3. Spacing Token Hierarchy
```typescript
// From smallest to largest:
xs: 4px    → Tight internal component spacing
sm: 8px    → Small gaps between related elements
md: 12px   → Medium gaps between sections within a card
base: 16px → Default spacing, screen gutter, header gap
lg: 20px   → Large gaps between major sections
xl: 24px   → Extra large section dividers
2xl: 32px  → Major content blocks
```

### 4. Consistency Checklist (REQUIRED for Every Screen)
When migrating any screen, verify:
- ✅ Uses `ScreenWrapper` (handles horizontal padding automatically)
- ✅ First content after Header has `marginTop: theme.spacing.headerContentGap`
- ✅ Major sections have consistent vertical spacing (`lg` or `xl`)
- ✅ Cards/components have consistent internal padding (`base` or `md`)
- ✅ NO hardcoded pixel values for spacing (use tokens)

### 5. Visual Consistency Principle
**"Same elements, same spacing, every screen."**
- Balance/Stats cards should have identical positioning patterns
- Feature sections should have matching gaps
- List items should have uniform spacing
- Button groups should maintain consistent padding

